Z||000000||bHooper||01-07-2001||09:36 PM||||since i finished reguilding the suspension on my GT, and having it aligned (-1 degree camber)... the car has developed a pull to the right.<P>today, i had to install some new ss brake lines, so it was the first oportunity to look at the front suspension.<P>boy was i surprised to see the condition of the right front upper control arm bushing... it was <B>mushroomed</B> at the point going into the tube!<P>i did not expect to see this.  has anyone ever seen that b4? <P>could that have anything to do with the pull?  <BR>when i reinstalled everything, there wasn't enough room to put the factory washers, both in front and behind the "tube", so i put one behind, and a 2 mm washer in front.<P>obtw, the drivers side looks normal, and is set up the exact same way.<P>thanks!<BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||3
