Z||000012||Oreif||01-09-2001||01:55 AM||||I was able to install all the washers and such when I did my car. Is there a way you could post a pic? If I remember correctly I had 4 large washers (about 2" in diameter)(2 for each bushing) and 2 caster shims that fit onto the control arm bolt. The way I assembled it was the bushings were not seated tightly to the ouside edge of the sleeve. They were flush with the inside edge of the sleeve. All washers and shims were installed then the long bolt was torqued. This seated the bushings so the outside edge was against the edge of the sleeve. If you seated the bushings to the outside of the sleeve first you couldn't get the washers in. Could this be what you mean? <BR>(mine is an 1986)<P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-09-2001).]||||reg||1
